    "Byte-identical requests hit (5/5); hits are 128-token aligned and exclude roughly the final message.",
    "Any change inside the system message (appended line, tool order, reminder moved or changed) gives 0 even with 1,000-1,944 identical leading tokens (K6, rev, tail, cur step-to-step).",
    "The current layout changes the system message on every call, so C cannot hit; B's fixed 1280-token hits equal floor((714+632+17)/128)*128, a shared tools+static prefix served by the provider that the probe could not reproduce (cur B-3 = 0) and that never occurred for C.",
    "With a stable system message and append-only history, implicit hits were still unreliable step-to-step (1 of 4).",
    "Explicit content-block markers hit deterministically: marker on the newest history message gives hits of the whole previous prefix with creation billed only for the delta (1949 -> 2272 -> 2394 cached; 323/122/144 created).",
    "Message-level cache_control, which AgentScope emits when cacheControl=true, is ignored by Bailian (xm: no creation, no hit)."
